The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
list_for_each_entry_safe(item, next, &list->head, list) {
    list_del(&item->list);
    kfree(item);
}
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because the driver attempts to free every item in the `purex_list`, including a pre-allocated structure (`item->vha->default_item`) that should not be freed. This results in an invalid memory access and a crash during module unload tests.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (item == &item->vha->default_item)
    continue;
```
Reason:
This code statement checks if the current item is the pre-allocated structure that should not be freed. If it is, the `continue` statement skips the `kfree(item)` call for that item, preventing the invalid memory access and subsequent kernel panic.

